laude\nts_utc: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ\ntype: claim|proposal|review|ack|status|decision|handoff\nack: false\ntask: T-001\nlead: codex\nfiles_owned:\n  - path/or/glob\n---\n\nTL;DR: one sentence.\n\nBody.\n\n- Codex\n```\n\nThe full message-type list and concurrency fields live in\n`coord/AGENTS_PROTOCOL.md`; that file is canonical.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Do not call the principal \"human\" in project-facing prose when a name is configured.\n- Do not commit or push unrelated WIP.\n- Do not edit files another agent has claimed unless the thread grants it.\n- Keep `STATE.md` short; use threads for details.\n- If disagreement loops twice, escalate to `coord/HUMAN.md`.\n- If using Codex subagents, the main Codex session owns protocol side effects:\n  post one claim/status/review for the batch, not one thread message per\n  subagent.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
